# Two constants naming each other. Each sits in the other's constructor
# slot, so both are guarded and both tie — the count of names a cycle runs
# through is not what decides it. Beside this, a_constant_that_names_itself
# ties the same two-node graph through one binding.
#
# Native reaches a knotted constant through its cell rather than its
# builder, and answers that cell as a value rather than as a register-held
# record: the cell carries a blackhole while the cycle is still building,
# and a record read in registers has nowhere to put a thunk.
type node
  id
  peer

pub ring = node 1 mate

mate = node 2 ring

pub play = print "{ring.peer.id} {ring.peer.peer.id} {ring.peer}"
